@page "/guidelines"

<PageTitle>Guidelines · Suttisak.Blazor UI Playbook</PageTitle>

<PlaybookShell>
    <main class="guidelines-page">
        <header class="guidelines-page__hero">
            <span class="playbook-kicker">Shared UI requirements</span>
            <h1>Component requirements</h1>
            <p>Shared components must work across themes, keyboard navigation, constrained containers, asynchronous states, and application content.</p>
        </header>

        <section class="guidelines-page__section" aria-labelledby="accessibility-guide-title">
            <header><span>01</span><div><h2 id="accessibility-guide-title">Accessibility</h2><p>Accessibility requirements are part of the component API.</p></div></header>
            <div class="guidelines-page__cards">
                <article><strong>Native elements</strong><p>Use the semantic HTML element that provides the expected browser and assistive-technology behavior.</p></article>
                <article><strong>Keyboard behavior</strong><p>Tab, Enter, Space, arrow keys, and Escape must follow the interaction model of the control.</p></article>
                <article><strong>Visible focus</strong><p>Every interactive state needs a visible focus indicator in product themes and forced-colors mode.</p></article>
                <article><strong>Semantic relationships</strong><p>Connect labels, descriptions, errors, headings, panels, and controls with semantic attributes.</p></article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="guidelines-page__section" aria-labelledby="theming-guide-title">
            <header><span>02</span><div><h2 id="theming-guide-title">Theming</h2><p>Products own identity. The library owns semantic roles and behavior.</p></div></header>
            <div class="guidelines-page__split">
                <div><h3>Library owns</h3><ul><li>Semantic token names</li><li>Component structure</li><li>Interaction behavior</li><li>Responsive contracts</li><li>Focus and feedback semantics</li></ul></div>
                <div><h3>Application owns</h3><ul><li>Brand color values</li><li>Copy and localization</li><li>Routes and authorization</li><li>Product imagery and marks</li><li>Domain-specific composition</li></ul></div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="guidelines-page__section" aria-labelledby="responsive-guide-title">
            <header><span>03</span><div><h2 id="responsive-guide-title">Responsive behavior</h2><p>Shared components should respond to the space they receive instead of assuming which device owns the page.</p></div></header>
            <div class="guidelines-page__checks">
                <span>375 px constrained preview</span><span>768 px constrained preview</span><span>Long localized content</span><span>200% text zoom</span><span>Reduced motion</span><span>Light and dark themes</span>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="guidelines-page__section" aria-labelledby="status-guide-title">
            <header><span>04</span><div><h2 id="status-guide-title">Component maturity</h2><p>Status indicates how much change consumers should expect.</p></div></header>
            <div class="guidelines-page__status-grid">
                <article><strong>Stable</strong><p>Suitable for normal use. Breaking changes require a migration.</p></article>
                <article><strong>Beta</strong><p>Available for use, but its API or composition may still change.</p></article>
                <article><strong>Experimental</strong><p>Intended for evaluation. Expect frequent changes.</p></article>
                <article><strong>Deprecated</strong><p>Existing consumers may remain temporarily, but new code should use the documented replacement.</p></article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="guidelines-page__section" aria-labelledby="documentation-guide-title">
            <header><span>05</span><div><h2 id="documentation-guide-title">Documentation model</h2><p>Components, executable stories, and composition patterns answer different questions and are counted separately.</p></div></header>
            <div class="guidelines-page__cards">
                <article><strong>@PlaybookComponentCatalog.All.Count components</strong><p>Each <code>/components/{slug}</code> page lists API details, source links, maturity, coverage, and related patterns.</p></article>
                <article><strong>@PlaybookSpecimenRegistry.InteractiveSpecimenCount mappings / @PlaybookSpecimenRegistry.DistinctSpecimenCount workbenches</strong><p>A specimen displays a component state or interaction. Several components may share a workbench.</p></article>
                <article><strong>@PlaybookPatternCatalog.All.Count patterns</strong><p>Each <a href="patterns">pattern</a> lists its components, assembly steps, responsibilities, sample Razor, page route, and tests.</p></article>
                <article><strong>Generated manifest</strong><p>The manifest is generated from the component and pattern catalogs. Contract tests compare it with the exported component types.</p></article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="guidelines-page__section guidelines-page__workflow" aria-labelledby="workflow-guide-title">
            <header><span>06</span><div><h2 id="workflow-guide-title">Repository workflow</h2><p>Use this sequence when adding or changing shared UI.</p></div></header>
            <ol>
                <li><strong>Search the component catalog.</strong><span>Check existing components and patterns before adding markup or another component.</span></li>
                <li><strong>Read the component page.</strong><span>Check its status, API, specimen, responsive behavior, and related patterns.</span></li>
                <li><strong>Check page patterns.</strong><span><code>/patterns</code> lists the components, assembly order, responsibilities, and page route.</span></li>
                <li><strong>Use semantic tokens.</strong><span>Reusable CSS must not contain a product palette.</span></li>
                <li><strong>Regenerate the manifest.</strong><span>Update the catalogs, then run <code>dotnet run --project scripts/PlaybookManifestGenerator/PlaybookManifestGenerator.csproj</code>.</span></li>
                <li><strong>Run the tests.</strong><span>Build the solution, run bUnit, and run the Playwright suite.</span></li>
            </ol>
            <a href="component-manifest.json">View component manifest →</a>
        </section>
    </main>
</PlaybookShell>
